          },
          "notes": "The library's defaults when its client is built without LLM, embedder or reranker clients: OpenAIClient (llm_client/openai_base_client.py DEFAULT_MODEL='gpt-5.5', DEFAULT_SMALL_MODEL='gpt-4.1-nano'; reasoning 'auto' resolves to effort 'none' for gpt-5.5), OpenAIEmbedder (embedder/openai.py DEFAULT_EMBEDDING_MODEL='text-embedding-3-small'; embedder/client.py EMBEDDING_DIM env default 1024, applied by truncating the returned vector), OpenAIRerankerClient (cross_encoder/openai_reranker_client.py DEFAULT_MODEL='gpt-4.1-nano', one logprob-scored chat call per candidate passage). The shim passes these same values explicitly so the record and the run cannot drift."
        },
        "common": {
          "model_roles": {
            "extraction": "gpt-4.1-mini",
            "small": "gpt-4.1-mini",
            "embedder": "text-embedding-3-large",
            "dims": 1536,
            "reranker": "gpt-4.1-nano"
          },
          "unsettable": [],
          "notes": "Both LLM roles (main and small) are set to gpt-4.1-mini. Dimensions are set the way the library sets them: OpenAIEmbedderConfig.embedding_dim truncates the 3,072-dimension text-embedding-3-large vector client-side (the API's `dimensions` parameter is never sent). The reranker is outside the common contract and stays at the recipe's gpt-4.1-nano."
        }
      },
      "time": "native",
      "time_notes": "add_episode(reference_time=session event_time). In message granularity each turn gets reference_time = event_time + turn_index milliseconds so retrieve_episodes (ORDER BY valid_at DESC) sees the conversation order instead of ties. search_ takes no query time, so query_time is ignored and applied_settings says so. An event_time or query_time without a UTC offset is read as UTC.",
      "granularity": "session (default, SHIM_GRANULARITY=session): one EpisodeType.message episode per session whose body is the session's 'speaker: text' lines. message (SHIM_GRANULARITY=message): one episode per turn, as the vendor's LoCoMo harness does. The metered smoke measures both; the preregistration fixes one.",
      "provenance": {
        "status": "partial",
        "mechanism": "Mixed by item class. Edges (facts): EntityEdge.episodes lists the episodes that produced or re-asserted the fact; episode uuids map to source ids through the episode name (source_id or source_id#turn) via EpisodicNode.get_by_uuids, provenance exact (partial if an episode was deleted). Entity nodes: EntityNode carries no episodes field at the pinned release (nodes.py:499-504); the public classmethod EpisodicNode.get_by_entity_node_uuid returns the episodes with a MENTIONS edge to the node, reported as partial because the node summary is rewritten per episode and need not reflect every mention. Set settings.node_provenance='none' to report entity nodes as unavailable. Episodes: exact (the episode itself). Communities: unavailable (none are built)."
      },
      "delete": "native",
      "delete_notes": "The library's remove_episode for every episode of the source (its client module, lines 1824-1855). Its semantics are the product's: it deletes edges whose FIRST episode is the removed one (even if later episodes re-asserted them), keeps edges first created by another episode (their episodes list keeps the removed uuid), and deletes entity nodes mentioned only by the removed episode. P2 measures the residue; the shim does not repair it.",
      "readiness": "synchronous: add_episode returns after extraction, resolution and writes; /finish has no background work to wait for",
      "namespace": "group_id (group_id = ns, one Neo4j database); reset = graph_data_operations.clear_data(driver, group_ids=[ns])",
      "parallel_namespaces": true,
      "retrieval_policies": {
        "vendor-default": {
          "settings": {
            "recipe": "COMBINED_HYBRID_SEARCH_CROSS_ENCODER",
            "limit": 10,
            "node_provenance": "mentions"
          },
          "notes": "The library's search_() with no config argument: COMBINED_HYBRID_SEARCH_CROSS_ENCODER (edges, nodes, episodes and communities; BM25 + cosine + BFS candidates, cross-encoder rerank) at SearchConfig's default limit 10 per class (search_config.py DEFAULT_SEARCH_LIMIT)."
        },
        "fixed-evidence": {
          "settings": {
            "recipe": "COMBINED_HYBRID_SEARCH_CROSS_ENCODER",
            "limit": 50,
            "node_provenance": "mentions"
          },
          "notes": "The same recipe with 50 results per class, enough to fill the 8,000-token evidence budget (facts run about 25 tokens, node summaries about 100); the harness packer truncates."
        },
        "allowed_settings_overrides": [
          "recipe (any upper-case name in the library's search.search_config_recipes module)",
          "limit",
          "node_provenance (mentions | none)"
        ],
        "vendor_benchmark_reference": {
          "searches": [
            {
              "scope": "nodes",
              "reranker": "rrf",
              "limit": 20,
              "recipe": "NODE_HYBRID_SEARCH_RRF"
            },
            {
              "scope": "edges",
              "reranker": "cross_encoder",
              "limit": 20,
              "recipe": "EDGE_HYBRID_SEARCH_CROSS_ENCODER"
            }
          ],
          "notes": "The vendor's LoCoMo harness (its search script) runs these two searches against the hosted service and renders facts as '<fact> (event_time: <valid_at>)' followed by entities as '<name>: <summary>'. Recorded for reference, not a shootout policy."
        },
        "item_mapping": "search_ returns separate ranked lists per class whose reranker scores are not on one scale, so the shim concatenates them in a fixed class order, each in temporal-graph's own rank order: edges, then entity nodes, then episodes, then communities (the vendor's harness also puts facts before entities). Edge -> type fact, text = fact, valid_from = valid_at, valid_to = invalid_at. Node -> type entity, text = '<name>: <summary>'. Episode -> type episode, text = content, valid_from = valid_at. Community -> type observation, text = '<name>: <summary>'. Raw per-class uuids and reranker scores are returned under raw."
      },
      "streaming": "disabled",
      "provider_routes": [
        "POST /v1/responses (structured extraction, responses.parse)",
        "POST /v1/chat/completions (cross-encoder reranker with logprobs)",
        "POST /v1/embeddings"
      ],
      "telemetry_off": [
        "GRAPHITI_TELEMETRY_ENABLED=false",
